# NIST RTTM. Ten whitespace-separated fields, decimal SECONDS.
#   Type FileID ChanID StartTime Duration Ortho Stype Name NoSpeakers Confidence
#
#   SPEAKER clip01 1   0.000000  8.400000 <NA> <NA> A <NA> <NA>
#   SPEAKER clip01 1   8.520000 11.900000 <NA> <NA> B <NA> <NA>
#
# Use your own labels. A permutation is resolved before anything is compared,
# so the harness never compares these strings.
#
# Merge adjacent stretches of the same person: two consecutive A records is a
# speaker change the human did not hear, and it will be counted against the
# reference.
#
# Cover the whole clip. A record that stops at a pause makes the hypothesis
# look like it is hallucinating through the silence.
#
# Record overlap as two records with identical start and end:
#   SPEAKER clip01 1 47.000000 3.100000 <NA> <NA> A <NA> <NA>
#   SPEAKER clip01 1 47.000000 3.100000 <NA> <NA> B <NA> <NA>
# The diarizer emits at most one speaker at a time, so every millisecond of
# overlap you record is a millisecond of DER it cannot avoid. Omitting it
# flatters the score for the wrong reason.
#
# Leave the silences out entirely. Do not write NOSPEAKER records.
